{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run an internal DNS resolver on node1 that resolves inventory-api.internal to node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 runs the preinstalled dnsmasq service on TCP and UDP port 53, with a persistent record mapping inventory-api.internal to node2 at 10.100.166.11. Both local and node2-originated queries received that answer, including after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-11f08feb269c4ace","cmd-1e46f6c9e0024458","cmd-c3c3725f4c6242fc","cmd-f2daed825aa64604"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure node2 to use node1 as its DNS resolver for internal lookups.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2's active resolver and persistent interface configuration point to node1 at 10.100.166.10. The system resolver successfully resolved inventory-api.internal to 10.100.166.11 before and after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1e46f6c9e0024458","cmd-267942e39bf04dd4","cmd-b31db15c2fb64c8c","cmd-d8f8871ed76440a1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS 5.11 with kernel 2.6.18-398.el5. Node1 used the already-installed CentOS 5 dnsmasq 2.45 package rather than replacing the operating system or kernel.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f6ad5f601e2f4624","cmd-a13ad03522954c69","cmd-f2daed825aa64604","cmd-d8f8871ed76440a1","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"No purposeless state-changing command was identified. The DNS configuration, service enablement, firewall rules, resolver changes, and restarts all had clear task or mandatory evidence-protocol roles. One minor hygiene defect remains: cmd-f526463e3863425c created /tmp/internal-dns.conf as a staging file that contributed to the final configuration, but the staging copy was not cleaned up and remained after execution. No unnecessary mutation was reverted or retained beyond that residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f526463e3863425c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered DNS behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently match the executor's before/after observations.","limitations":["The generic after-executor listening-socket snapshot was empty even though direct executor commands showed dnsmasq listening on node1; the direct service and query evidence is substantially more specific, but the discrepancy prevents perfect confidence.","The legacy lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation both before and after execution, so package consistency was not independently validated."]}
